## Test naming

The TC ID is where the runner reports it (`test-case-traceability.md`):

```
component:   describe('<ScreenName>', () => { it('TC-MCMP-20112 shows <state> when <condition>') })
device flow: .maestro/TC-ME2E-20101-<workflow>.yaml      name: "TC-ME2E-20101 <workflow>"
platform:    .maestro/platform/TC-MPLT-20103-<behaviour>.yaml   name: "TC-MPLT-20103 <behaviour>"
```

## Iteration rules

- A test failing because the **app** is wrong stays committed and failing. Record it in
  `bugs_found[]` (screen, TC ID, platform, expected vs actual) for `mobile_developer`. You never
  edit app code.
- A test that is wrong is fixed without weakening it: never weaken an assertion, add `.skip`/`.only`,
  or raise a timeout to make a test pass (develop-orchestrator Test Failure Recovery Guardrails).
  When you fix it, put the why and when on one line directly above every change to a test that existed before this
  phase: `// TEST-CHANGE <YYYY-MM-DD> phase <N>: <why> (spec: <ref> | moved: <where the check lives now>)`. A changed or removed assertion must cite `spec:` or `moved:`. A deleted test
  file goes in `agent_state/phases/{{PHASE}}/test-changes.json` with a reason. `tc-inventory.py
  --diff-base` fails any change without one (`~/.claude/skills/testing/test-case-traceability.md` §Changing an existing test).
  Maximum 3 attempts, then report it.
- A test that passes only on retry is FLAKY. Report it with the retry count, never as PASS. Flaky
  counts as failing at the gate.

## Evidence (what the gate reads — skills/testing/test-results-sidecar.md)

The Node tiers (Tiers 1, 2 and the component part of 5):

```bash
P="agent_state/phases/{{PHASE}}"; mkdir -p "$P/junit" "$P/reports"
git add {{MOBILE_APP_DIR}} && git commit -m "phase {{PHASE}}: mobile tests + flows (TC-…)"   # commit first
CMD="$(jq -r '.commands["x:mobile-jest"]' agent_state/config/verify-commands.json)"
[ -n "$CMD" ] && [ "$CMD" != null ] || { echo "BLOCKED: no x:mobile-jest command in verify-commands.json (jest --ci with jest-junit → $P/junit/mobile-jest.xml)"; exit 1; }
PHASE={{PHASE}} bash -c "$CMD" > "$P/junit/mobile-jest.log" 2>&1; RC=$?
python3 .claude/hooks/junit-to-sidecar.py --tier mobile --command "$CMD" --exit-code $RC \
  --priorities "$P/tc_priorities.json" --out "$P/reports/mobile_test_results.json" "$P/junit/mobile-jest.xml"
```

No retries to green. The device flows' evidence is `mobile_e2e_orchestrator`'s
`mobile_e2e_results.json`, per platform. Your local run of a flow is a dry-run.

